+### 3b. Stored branch status (migration 0044)
+
+A branch's settlement is a *stored column* on `memory_map_membership` — the
+single source of truth for "settled". An `edge` row in `memory_references`
+(e.g. `resolves-under`) is only a *link*, never a settlement signal.
+
+```
+memory_map_membership
+  status              text not null default 'open'  -- open | resolved | dropped
+  resolution_summary  text null  -- 1-500 chars, set iff status != 'open'
+  resolved_by_memory_id uuid null references memories(id) on delete set null
+  resolved_by_party   text null check (in ('owner','model'))
+  resolved_at         timestamptz null
+```
+
+A consistency CHECK enforces: `open` ⟺ all resolution fields IS NULL; non-open
+⟹ resolution_summary NOT NULL, resolved_by_party NOT NULL, resolved_at NOT NULL.
+The cursor-read index `memory_map_events_cursor_idx(root_memory_id, id)` supports
+cheap incremental reads. `mindmap_resolve` sets these columns in place;
+`mindmap_get` reads them.
+
